**Day 32: MongoDB – Installation & Basics**  

**Topic:**  
Introduction to MongoDB, its document-based structure, and BSON format. Installation and initial setup of MongoDB and MongoDB Compass.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand MongoDB as a NoSQL database.  
• Learn about documents, collections, and BSON format.  
• Install MongoDB and MongoDB Compass for database management.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Install MongoDB 7 and MongoDB Compass.  
• Create a sample database and collection.  
• Explore basic operations using the MongoDB shell.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• **Documents:** Data stored in JSON-like format (BSON).  
• **Collections:** Groups of documents, analogous to tables in SQL.  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `use <database>` – Switch to or create a database.  
• `db.createCollection("<collection>")` – Create a new collection.  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Storing unstructured or semi-structured data (e.g., user profiles, logs).  
• Scalable applications requiring flexible schema design.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• MongoDB 7  
• MongoDB Compass (GUI for MongoDB)  

**Summary:**  
Today covered MongoDB basics, including installation, document structure, and initial database setup. Hands-on practice included creating databases and collections using both CLI and Compass.  

